 I think he can help a lot of  people by having Gobert follow-through  with a PSA and I also think you know I'm  interested in how Donovan Mitchell feels  and how quickly he can get by maybe Joe  bears recklessness putting him in  jeopardy and his teammates in jeopardy I  think that's another interesting sort of  subplot to the whole thing but I think  oh bear took took the right first step  by just acknowledging what he did wrong  there was no excuse for it and he wants  to help in any way possible going  forward before I let you go Jeff Van  Gundy I'll ask you a question I asked  both Jay Bilas and our number one in  Michigan State's Tom Izzo and our number  two I'd love to get the perspective of  somebody from the next level the the  idea that Geno Auriemma threw out  yesterday upon the announcement that the  NCAA tournaments for men and women's  basketball had been canceled  that seniors should get an extra year  the the seniors right now that they're  their senior years should not end like  this if they so choose to get another  year of eligibility I wonder what you  think of that idea I think it's a  reaction in the immediate aftermath of a  disappointing thing that occurs in these  young people's lives and I feel  for all the college athletes it's not  just the Division one athletes it's the  division three and two tournaments or  going on you know you have spring sports  that have just gotten off the ground  that now they won't be able to compete  in their senior year and while I  understand the idea behind giving them  an extra year and I wouldn't be opposed  to it I also think one of the things  you're constantly trying to teach young  people is stuff happens in life and bad  stuff happens in life and it's not what  happens to you it's what you do next and  so if the NCAA ultimately decides not to  do or the giving the extra year of  eligibility back to these you know I  think spring sports is different than  winter sports because they didn't  actually compete in the get a chance to  compete in those sport I would have no  no problem with the NCAA no it's a bad  thing we feel badly but you need to move  on and deal with it and for the spring  sports I understand why there may be an  exception granted for that because they  didn't get a chance to even play their  regular season Jeff thanks for the time  stay safe be safe be healthy and I hope  we get you back on in April and we'll  talk about an NBA star basketball yeah I  look forward to it I appreciate the time  though today thanks for the call be well  your family - you bet that's Jeff Van  Gundy

